<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Boniak</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 1090s–1100s</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Bonyak</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Boniak was a Cuman khan of the late 11th and early 12th centuries, notorious in the Rus' chronicles for his raids on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a> and the surrounding lands, including the sack of the Kyiv Caves Monastery in 1096. In 1099 he helped a Rus' prince defeat a Hungarian army in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a>. He was a frequent target of the steppe campaigns led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladimir-ii-monomakh">Vladimir Monomakh</a>.</p></div>
